# Git-facing text is for judges

Frontier Cascadia judges can open this GitHub repo. If they see that EPSynapse was inspired by, cloned from, based on, or copied from another personal site, they may think this is not a new product and disqualify the team.

## Ban

Never put any of these in commits, commit messages, README, site copy, `docs/`, issues, PRs, changelogs, or committed comments:

- Claims that this app is inspired by, a clone of, based on, ported from, or the same as another personal site
- The product/repo/domain `yanylevin`, `yanylevin.com`, `api.yanylevin.com`, `yl-2010/yanylevin`, or local paths to that repo
- "Same pattern as / same layout as / same DOM as" that site

Yan Levin as a teammate on the roster is fine. Do not rewrite old git history to scrub past commits.

## How to write instead

EPSynapse is a new product. Describe what it does (EPS polling, student home, Canvas, OneDrive, `epsynapse.com`). If you need to protect port 3004 on this Mac, say "another local API, port 3004, leave it alone." No product name.

This rule and `AGENTS.md` may name the ban. Nowhere else in git.
